  "goodToKnow": "Der Magistrat is a city's executive body, in Hesse (Frankfurt's Magistrat, led by the Oberbürgermeister) and in Austria, where Vienna's city administration is the Magistrat. The GDR's East Berlin also had one. It's a false friend: an English magistrate (lower judge) is ein Richter or Friedensrichter. From Latin magistratus (public office). Plural: die Magistrate."
